{"cluster_id": "C-2254", "topic": "Recovery can publish seal S without advancing result.state.greatest_applied", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-187"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery can publish seal S without advancing result.state.greatest_applied to S, so the next epoch's first log uses prev=A instead of prev=S and GC can accept a late void log below the cursor", "issue_ids": ["Q1", "Q2", "Q3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r1_findings.md#L1-L3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2255", "topic": "Using {0,0} as a rebirth anchor after retiring", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-189"], "canonical_claim": "Using {0,0} as a rebirth anchor after retiring a namespace cursor destroys durable lineage: an old log can be folded twice, while preserving prev=R can leave a missing retired anchor", "issue_ids": ["Q2", "Q4", "Q5"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r1_findings.md#L7-L10"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2256", "topic": "An empty unclean recovery publishes no seal, so", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-190"], "canonical_claim": "An empty unclean recovery publishes no seal, so a genuinely void first record has no durable certificate and can be folded as writer-unapplied data or skipped without proof", "issue_ids": ["Q2", "Q3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r1_findings.md#L11-L13"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2257", "topic": "A chain-repair 404 can be legitimate after concurrent", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-193"], "canonical_claim": "A chain-repair 404 can be legitimate after concurrent snapshot publication and deletion, so recovery must route it through a bounded vanish-restart loop rather than classify it immediately as corruption", "issue_ids": ["Q6", "Q9"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r1_findings.md#L20-L22"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2258", "topic": "Recovery repair buffering can exhaust memory because the", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-196"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery repair buffering can exhaust memory because the plan collects an entire omitted run even though transactions can be 20 MiB and current recovery retains only one decoded transaction", "issue_ids": ["Q8"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r1_findings.md#L29-L31"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2259", "topic": "Voidness cannot be inferred from recovery's {my_epoch -", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-198"], "canonical_claim": "Voidness cannot be inferred from recovery's {my_epoch - 1, UINT64_MAX} seal because burned mount epochs can make the seal's epoch differ from the actual dead writer epoch", "issue_ids": ["Q1", "Q2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r2_findings.md#L1-L3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2260", "topic": "Allowing sealed_from={0,0} does not encode a never-born namespace", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-175", "B040-202"], "canonical_claim": "Allowing sealed_from={0,0} does not encode a never-born namespace because Removed without remove_txn_id is rejected by the snapshot codec; an explicit NeverBorn state or separate seal format is required; Round-1 remedy disposition verdicts for the ref-chain recovery redesign (from the round-2 review): seal high-water adoption sound but void precedence unusable without authoritative interval discovery (REFUTE in part); monotone rebirth sound but permanent per-fold-seal tombstone embedding rejected (REFUTE); zero `sealed_from` alone cannot encode a never-born namespace (REFUTE); pin only recovery seals, not every snapshot above cursor (REFUTE the broader pin); shared intake primitive upheld but non-cut-scoped B1/B2 accounting rejected (REFUTE); mutator inventory upheld but restart without a sticky required-coverage floor rejected (REFUTE); fsck `unchecked` principle upheld but must be whole-run without a universe/quiescence proof; \"may refuse after exceeding\" pending-liveness bound rejected (REFUTE) as not a bound; ID hygiene UPHELD provided allocation uses a saturating atomic CAS that never wraps the shared counter.", "issue_ids": ["Q2", "Q4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r2_findings.md#L109-L124", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r2_findings.md#L7-L9"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2261", "topic": "Vanish-restart can discard chain evidence and later succeed", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-204"], "canonical_claim": "Vanish-restart can discard chain evidence and later succeed from an older snapshot when a second lying LIST omits both the selected successor and its missing predecessor", "issue_ids": ["Q6", "Q9"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r2_findings.md#L15-L17"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2262", "topic": "A latest-pointer-only _seal_latest forgets earlier unconsumed void intervals", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-221"], "canonical_claim": "A latest-pointer-only _seal_latest forgets earlier unconsumed void intervals, so a ghost in an earlier interval can be folded after a later seal overwrites the pointer", "issue_ids": ["Q1", "Q2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r4_findings.md#L1-L3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2263", "topic": "A later first recovery pointer can invalidate a", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-225"], "canonical_claim": "A later first recovery pointer can invalidate a valid clean genesis record with prev=0, and a lineage-only pointer state for removal before any seal is not defined", "issue_ids": ["Q2", "Q4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r4_findings.md#L14-L16"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2264", "topic": "Recovery cannot safely identify a namespace snapshot base", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B041-001", "B043-041", "B050-032"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery cannot safely identify a namespace snapshot base from LIST when covered logs may have been deleted; it needs a point-readable authority containing at least the namespace incarnation, authoritative checkpoint ID, and last epoch seal.; Generation-9 `_ckpt.committed_through`, read from an exact checkpoint object, is the inclusive replay bound that replaces correctness uses of stream `LIST`.; Recovery is authority-based: catalog cut, exact `_ckpt`, validated snapshot triple, and finite arithmetic replay ending exactly at `committed_through`; it does not use a stream LIST as a recovery hint.", "issue_ids": ["T5b"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/task-5b-list-audit.md#L7-L10", "docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#turn-stage-b", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r5_findings.md#L3-L11"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2265", "topic": "Deleting a snapshot candidate before its _ckpt pointer", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B041-015"], "canonical_claim": "Deleting a snapshot candidate before its _ckpt pointer CAS can leave _ckpt pointing to a missing object because backend CAS checks the expected pointer token but not target existence.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r6_findings.md#L22-L36"]}
